<header><p class="st-kicker">prince bishopric · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Prince-Bishopric of Cammin</h1><p class="st-meta">1248 CE – 1650 CE (approx.) · capital Köslin</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Pomeranian church state founded as the bishopric of the newly converted Pomeranians and secularised into a Brandenburg principality in 1650.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The bishopric of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-pomerania">Pomerania</a> was founded in 1140 at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolin">Wolin</a> after the mission of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-of-bamberg">Otto of Bamberg</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adalbert-of-pomerania">Adalbert</a> as first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a>, and moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamien-pomorski">Cammin</a> by 1176. Exempt from any archbishop, it answered directly to the pope. In 1248 the bishops acquired the land of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kolobrzeg">Kolberg</a>, forming their secular territory with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koszalin">Köslin</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bobolice">Bublitz</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> ruled a small but distinct territory, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koszalin">Köslin</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kolobrzeg">Kolberg</a> its main towns and residences. They claimed imperial immediacy, which the dukes of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-pomerania">Pomerania</a> contested, and the Pomeranian estates drew the bishopric into ducal politics. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> in the 1530s the see became Lutheran and was administered by members of the Pomeranian ducal house.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The last administrator, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ernst-bogislaw-von-croy">Ernst Bogislaw of Croÿ</a>, handed it over after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-westphalia">Peace of Westphalia</a> gave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamien-pomorski">Cammin</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a>, which took possession in 1650 as the Principality of Cammin. The region has been part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> since 1945.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/prince-bishopric-of-cammin.jpg" alt="Prince-Bishopric of Cammin" width="320" height="240"><figcaption>Image: myself (User:Piotrus) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kamien_Pomorski_-_katedra_zewnatrz_07.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1248 CE – 1650 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>prince bishopric</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Köslin</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Adalbert of Pomerania, Ernst Bogislaw of Croÿ</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism, then Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Low German, Pomeranian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/poland">Poland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kamień, Hochstift Cammin</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1449&amp;focus=prince-bishopric-of-cammin" aria-label="Prince-Bishopric of Cammin on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5007 325 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Prince-Bishopric of Cammin lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5327 581L5324 597M5327 581L5282 625"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5324 597h0M5282 625h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5327 581h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5327 581h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1449&amp;focus=prince-bishopric-of-cammin">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
